<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abimilki</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">14th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century-bce">14th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abimilki was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tyre">Tyre</a> in the 14th century BCE, during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akhetaten">Amarna</a> period, when the city was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>. About ten of his letters to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pharaoh">pharaoh</a>, almost certainly <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akhenaten">Akhenaten</a>, survive among the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amarna-letters">Amarna letters</a>. In them he professes loyalty, reports news from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/levant">Levant</a> and complains that the king of Sidon has cut his island city off from water, wood and supplies.</p></div>
